vcl: a close request on a tooltip no longer uses the disposed tooltip.

ImplHandleClose first ends popups and help windows. When the close request was addressed to the
quick-help tooltip itself, ImplDestroyHelpWindow disposes that window, and the following
ImplGetWindow() dereferenced its cleared WindowImpl (SIGSEGV in vcl::Window::ImplGetWindow, seen
with the Templates and Fontwork Gallery dialogs when a test harness closed every new top-level
window, tooltips included). Stop when the addressed window is disposed.

Test: CppunitTest_vcl_lifecycle (HstHelpWindowCloseTest).
---
--- a/vcl/source/window/winproc.cxx
+++ b/vcl/source/window/winproc.cxx
@@ -2280,7 +2280,8 @@
     if (pSVData->mpWinData->mpTrackWin)
         pSVData->mpWinData->mpTrackWin->EndTracking( TrackingEventFlags::Cancel | TrackingEventFlags::Key );
 
-    if (bWasPopup)
+    // HST Office: a close request sent to a tooltip has just disposed it with the help windows
+    if (bWasPopup || pWindow->isDisposed())
         return;
 
     vcl::Window *pWin = pWindow->ImplGetWindow();
